@startuml
title 05 - User Management (Overview)
autonumber

actor "Frontend / Postman" as FE
participant "Gateway :8099" as GW
participant "Setting Service :8092" as SET
database "Setting DB" as SDB

group 1) Reference Data
  FE -> GW: POST /api/v1/setting/users/reference-data
  GW -> SET: Forward
  SET -> SDB: Load companies/roles/statuses/policies/privileges
  SET --> FE: reference-data
end

group 2) Add User
  FE -> GW: POST /api/v1/setting/users\n(actor username + newUsername + password + profile)
  GW -> SET: Forward
  SET -> SDB: Validate + insert user + default user_company
  SET --> FE: created profile
end

group 3) View / Update / Status
  FE -> GW: POST /api/v1/setting/users/view {id}
  GW -> SET: Forward
  SET -> SDB: Find user by id
  SET --> FE: profileDetails (newUsername)

  FE -> GW: POST /api/v1/setting/users/update {id,...}
  GW -> SET: Forward
  SET -> SDB: Update profile + role/company mapping sync
  SET --> FE: updated profile

  FE -> GW: POST /api/v1/setting/users/status {id,status}
  GW -> SET: Forward
  SET -> SDB: Update status + loginStatus rule
  SET --> FE: updated profile
end

group 4) Filter List
  FE -> GW: POST /api/v1/setting/users/filter-list\n(search.newUsername, role, nic, ...)
  GW -> SET: Forward
  SET -> SDB: Filter + sort + paginate
  SET --> FE: content[] + totalRecords\n(content uses newUsername)
end

group 5) Profile Image
  FE -> GW: POST /api/v1/setting/users/profile-image/update\n(base64 file payload)
  GW -> SET: Forward
  SET -> SDB: Save file doc + fileName + fileType + type
  SET --> FE: updated profileImg
end

note over FE
Detailed split diagrams:
- 05a-user-reference-data.puml
- 05b-user-add.puml
- 05c-user-view.puml
- 05d-user-update-status.puml
- 05e-user-filter-list.puml
- 05f-user-profile-image.puml
end note

@enduml
